1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,000
Explore Thread: find pieces, plan outfits
and arrange local clothing exchanges.

2
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:12,000
Annotated sample-data screens; not a
continuous live API recording.

3
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:18,000
Choose Explore the demo to open the sample
wardrobe in the local app.

4
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:24,000
Register and activate your email. Social
login needs server setup.

5
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:29,000
Browse your clothes and shoes, then open a
piece to inspect its details.

6
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:34,000
Favorite useful pieces, search by name, or
change the sorting order.

7
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:38,000
Select Blue to narrow this sample wardrobe
from 11 pieces to 3.

8
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:42,000
You can combine color with season, style,
era and favorites.

9
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:46,000
Add the Tops category: Blue + Tops leaves
one matching denim shirt.

10
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:50,000
Reset or clear the filters to return to
the complete collection.

11
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:56,000
Edit the category, color, season, style,
era and bundled photo.

12
00:00:56,000 --> 00:01:02,000
Mark unavailable pieces, then save your
changes in the complete local app.

13
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:07,500
For this example, choose All seasons,
Neutral and Quiet essentials.

14
00:01:07,500 --> 00:01:13,000
The engine combines an available top,
bottom and pair of shoes.

15
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:19,000
These example suggestions were exported
from the real C# API.

16
00:01:19,000 --> 00:01:25,000
Review the reasons, name a look and save
locally. Scores rank combinations.

17
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:29,500
Saved looks keep your favorite
combinations together under a useful name.

18
00:01:29,500 --> 00:01:34,000
Open Share outfit to manage a public link
for one look.

19
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:39,500
In the local app, create a share link and
copy it or share on social networks.

20
00:01:39,500 --> 00:01:45,000
Anyone with the link can view the outfit.
Revoke it to disable the old link.

21
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:51,000
Browse clothes to buy, borrow or receive,
or publish a listing locally.

22
00:01:51,000 --> 00:01:57,000
Request a reservation for local handover.
No online payments or shipping.

23
00:01:57,000 --> 00:02:03,000
Buyers request or cancel. Sellers accept,
decline or complete an exchange.

24
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:09,000
This sample reservation is already
accepted; use its details for handover.

25
00:02:09,000 --> 00:02:14,000
Manage your profile, password and sign-out
in the local app.

26
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:19,000
Development demo mode can switch between
the sample buyer and seller.

27
00:02:19,000 --> 00:02:25,000
Use the bottom navigation to reach all
five sections on your phone.

28
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:31,000
Expand Filters, set your choices and
return to the wardrobe grid.

29
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:36,000
The mobile editor keeps photos and garment
properties in a scrollable form.

30
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:41,000
Availability and favorite choices sit
above the save action.

31
00:02:41,000 --> 00:02:46,000
Move between Outfit studio and your saved
looks using the bottom bar.

32
00:02:46,000 --> 00:02:51,000
React adapts the layout; Redux keeps
interface choices between sections.

33
00:02:51,000 --> 00:02:57,000
Install .NET 10 SDK, Node.js 24 and Git,
then follow the commands shown.

34
00:02:57,000 --> 00:03:03,000
Open localhost:3000 and choose Explore the
demo.

35
00:03:03,000 --> 00:03:09,000
Build along with the workbook: C# MVC,
CQRS, EF Core SQLite, React and Redux.
